- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** Copy experiments from another kit… in the kit bar: the verb and the panel that picks the experiments (001 §O 'Kit menu'; 'Automation': every new control gets a stable id; .spec-md §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; AGENTS.md: every control of every window can be scrolled fully on screen). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the kit-bar group (step 188), each member with a one-line doc: `kitCopyExperimentsButton` (`"KitCopyExperimentsButton"`), `kitCopySourceText` (`"KitCopySourceText"`), `kitCopyExperimentList` (`"KitCopyExperimentList"`), `kitCopyChosenButton` (`"KitCopyChosenButton"`) and `kitCopyCancelButton` (`"KitCopyCancelButton"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `attachDataFile` (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:65`): `static member kitCopyExperimentToggle (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` = `KitCopyExperimentToggle_<n>`, with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, docs one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: the Kit menu gains, after Show in Explorer (001 §O's order), the verb `Copy experiments from another kit…` (`MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` carrying `kitCopyExperimentsButton`), present when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlOffered` (step 185) and `kitCopyOpt` is `None`; its press calls `model.kitShell.kitPicker.pickThen (OpenCopySource >> dispatch)` (steps 174, 225). When `kitCopyOpt` is `Some src`, under the verb row and any send progress: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitCopySourceText`, `Copy from <src.source.kitFile.name>: choose the experiments to copy.`; a `ScrollViewer` carrying `kitCopyExperimentList`, vertical scroll bar `Auto`, `MaxHeight` 160, over a vertical `StackPanel` of one `CheckBox` per experiment of `src.experiments`, each carrying `kitCopyExperimentToggle e.id`, its content `E<n> — <e.description>`, checked when `src.chosen` holds its id, and each change sending `ToggleCopiedExperiment e.id`; and one horizontal `StackPanel` of two `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton`s: `Copy` (`kitCopyChosenButton`, `positiveBackground`, `CopyChosenExperiments`), present only when `src.chosen` is not empty, and `Cancel` (`kitCopyCancelButton`, `negativeBackground`, `CloseCopySource`), the action box's right margin being the gap. The list scrolls inside its own height because the bar sits outside the page's `ScrollViewer` (step 188): a source of many experiments never pushes a control out of reach. Every id is an AutomationId. Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184), screens mounted as step 188's: without a trait, `the copy UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five fixed ids' texts and `kitCopyExperimentToggle (ExperimentId 3)`'s text `KitCopyExperimentToggle_3`. `an open source lists its experiments with a toggle each, and Copy and Cancel share a row, Cancel to the right` : over a model whose `kitCopyOpt` holds a source context from a folder kit with E1 and E2 and E2 chosen, `kitCopySourceText` names the source kit, E1's toggle is unchecked and E2's checked, and `kitCopyChosenButton` and `kitCopyCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel's left beyond Copy's right; with nothing chosen `kitCopyChosenButton` is absent. `a kit opened read-only offers no Copy experiments`: over the kit opened read-only `kitCopyExperimentsButton` is absent, and over it opened read-write present. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing at a box's centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit`: over a shell whose `kitPicker` answers a source kit folder holding E2 (made by `openKitAt` and closed), pressing `kitCopyExperimentsButton` shows the panel; pressing E2's toggle and then `kitCopyChosenButton` removes the panel, shows `kitStatus` starting `Copied 1 experiment(s)` and leaves `E2.experiment-json` in the window's kit folder. `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable` (step 188) keeps its assertion over a model that also runs a send (`kitSend` started and progressed) and holds an open copy source of forty experiments, so the bar is at its tallest.

**Acceptance.** After the copy panel lands, `kitCopyExperimentsButton` MUST open the folder dialog for a kit opened read-write, and an open source MUST list its experiments with a toggle each and Copy / Cancel on one row inside a bounded list; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the copy UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `an open source lists its experiments with a toggle each, and Copy and Cancel share a row, Cancel to the right`, `a kit opened read-only offers no Copy experiments` and the changed `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
